While loops
===========

`while cond` repeatedly runs the body while the cond
evaluates to true. `break` exits, `continue` skips to the
next iteration's cond evaluation.

    module sysl.tests.lang_features

Counted while loop
------------------

    #test
    test_counted_while() -> unit
        var i = 0
        var sum = 0
        while i < 10
            sum = sum + i
            i = i + 1
        // 0+1+...+9 = 45
        assert(sum == 45, s"sum 0..9 should be 45, got $sum")

While with break
----------------

    #test
    test_while_break() -> unit
        var i = 0
        while i < 100
            if i == 7 then break
            i = i + 1
        assert(i == 7, s"i should be 7 after break, got $i")

While with continue
-------------------

Skip iteration when condition holds; sum only even numbers.

    #test
    test_while_continue() -> unit
        var i = 0
        var sum = 0
        while i < 10
            i = i + 1
            if i % 2 == 1 then continue
            sum = sum + i
        // 2 + 4 + 6 + 8 + 10
        assert(sum == 30, s"sum of even 1..10 should be 30, got $sum")

Loop with body that never runs
------------------------------

    #test
    test_while_never_runs() -> unit
        var iterations = 0
        while false
            iterations = iterations + 1
        assert(iterations == 0, s"loop should not iterate, got $iterations")

Nested while loops
------------------

    #test
    test_nested_whiles() -> unit
        var total = 0
        var i = 0
        while i < 3
            var j = 0
            while j < 4
                total = total + 1
                j = j + 1
            i = i + 1
        // 3 * 4 = 12 iterations
        assert(total == 12, s"total should be 12, got $total")
